Packaging prebsd for Distributions
==================================

This file is for distribution packagers who want to add prebsd to their
distro's package repository.  Template packaging files for several systems
are provided under `packaging/`.  Each is roughly 90% complete — the packager
fills in maintainer details, changelog, and distro-specific adjustments.

What prebsd Is
--------------

prebsd fetches and runs Research Unix V4, V5, V6, V7 and 32V on SIMH (the
`pdp11` and `vax780` simulators), driving the console over telnet.  It ships
two tools: `fetch` (download/unpack a disk image from the `images.json`
manifest) and `boot.py` (the console driver).

Dependencies
------------

Runtime only — prebsd is a set of scripts, nothing is compiled:
  - python3 (boot.py)
  - curl (fetch)
  - simh with the `pdp11` simulator (V4-V7); 32V additionally needs `vax780`
    (the default Debian `simh` builds only MicroVAX, so compile `vax780`)

How the Build Works
-------------------

    ./configure && make && make install

`configure` is shipped, so autoconf/automake are not needed to build.

Install layout (default prefix `/usr/local`):

    $(bindir)/prebsd-fetch     symlink to $(libdir)/prebsd/fetch
    $(libdir)/prebsd/          fetch, boot.py, images.json, ini/
    $(mandir)/man1/            fetch.1, boot.1

